# A built Rust tree is far larger than its source, and the whole build
# context is uploaded to the builder. Without this, every deploy ships
# target/ across the wire.
operator/target/
target/
.git/
.github/

# Secrets. `COPY . .` uploads the context to whichever local or remote
# BuildKit builder runs the build, and it is cached there — so a file
# excluded from git is NOT thereby excluded from disclosure. Docker does
# not read .gitignore, which means every secret-bearing pattern in it
# has to be repeated here or it silently stops being secret at the
# moment this repo becomes a build context.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's `*.env` (its `!*.env.example` exception is
# deliberately not mirrored: an example file is harmless in the context
# and reproducing the negation is a way to get the pattern wrong).
.env
*.env
*.seed
deploy/discovery/provider.seed

# Publishing artifacts and fetched manifests: output, not input.
deploy/discovery/out/
deploy/discovery/reviewed/
